"│Chapters                ││    RAM is much faster than any disk. When a program│"
"│1. Filesystem           ││    reads a file, Linux keeps a copy in the page    │"
"│2. Disk                 ││    cache, so the next read comes straight from     │"
"│3. Permissions          ││    memory. Empty RAM does nothing for you, so the  │"
"│4. Processes & scheduli…││    kernel fills it with cache and takes it back    │"
"│  4.1 Process states an…││    when programs ask for memory.                   │"
"│5. Memory               ││                                                    │"
"│  5.1 free vs available ││    Taking cache back is cheap when the data is     │"
"│6. Finding and transfor…││    unchanged: it's still on disk, the kernel can   │"
"│  6.1 find              ││    drop it. Changed ("dirty") data must be written │"
"│                        ││    to disk first, which is slower.                 │"
